# The coworld-ctf commit the local simulator builds its engine from.
#
# This is a MEASUREMENT pin, not a convenience pin. The number the simulator
# prints is only comparable to a hosted result if the rules it stepped are the
# rules the league stepped, so this should track the source commit of the
# coworld package the league is actually running -- the same commit
# `bot/baseline/labels.nim` records itself verified against. The Observatory
# reports it:
#
#     coworld show <coworld_id> --json   # .manifest.game.runnable.source_url
#
# When you move this pin: re-sync labels.nim from the same commit, re-extract
# sim/league_config.json from that commit's coworld_manifest.json (the hosted
# variant's game_config, NOT the repo's config.json -- they disagree, and the
# manifest is what runs), and re-run `sim/selfcheck.sh`.
#
# Verified 2026-08-03 against coworld package `ctf` v0.7.173 (the canonical
# coworld's manifest source_url, read off a live league episode). The previous
# pin (1047232f, GV30, verified 2026-07-31) was FIVE game versions behind the
# league: GV31 grew the grenade blast to a body test (on-axis reach 52 -> 58)
# and the spray cone to five squares (136 -> 170), GV32 made a capture
# eliminate its team, GV33 takes a dead team's heart out of play, GV34 added
# per-shot Gaussian aim jitter, and GV35 stopped counting elimination deaths
# as combat deaths. game_config is NOT byte-identical across this move:
# visionConeDeg 45 -> 60, and lobbyJoinTimeoutTicks is new.

repo   https://github.com/Metta-AI/coworld-ctf
commit 63ea0cb74479a749600e5fa6da82ab9ac0f7c60e
